0 // Technic Differential with One Gear 28 Tooth Bevel: a 28 tooth bevel ring between z = 20
0 // and 28, its teeth facing -z, their cone's tip at z = -10 (measured from the LDraw shape),
0 // and a post inside for the middle (planet) bevel gear to turn on. The shadow library closes
0 // the holes the output axles go in at one end, and the post, so neither takes an axle or a
0 // gear's hole; they're open here. (Official models set a 20 tooth bevel gear 40 LDU out, its
0 // axle crossing the differential's at its middle, where neither cone's tip is: its tip is 10
0 // LDU out from there, the ring's 10 LDU the other way, so their cones touch along a line.)
